    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60d56758_dc7b0cb2",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 885,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-08T15:27:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we really need to save the list of handles? The information about what is a lend can be found in the host stage-2.\n\nOn a lend, we would do host_donate_ffa(). During reclaim, we could just check in the host stage-2 who owns the page? If it is FFA_OWNED, we then need to re-map it?",
      "revId": "39d5d9e55c8a360656ab9f30465fa9563b4a40d4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6cd9815f_8cb2250b",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 885,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T11:04:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we can avoid saving the list of handles I am all in favour of dropping it.\n\n`The information about what is a lend can be found in the host stage-2.` - yes I agree to your point. But we still have to keep handles because of the ffa fragmentation:\n\nWhen we have an sglist memory description that exceeds the size of the buffers, a caller decides to split the description into multiple transactions (fragments) and it goes like this:\n\n1. first transaction is an `smc` with `FFA_MEM_SHARE` or `FFA_MEM_LEND` with the length set to a slice of the total transfer. In a successful return to that we get a handle.\n2. The handle is used in a subsequent ffa-fragment call and at this stage the hypervisor needs to know whether the handle refers to a share or a lend. That\u0027s why I need to keep the handle around.\n\nWhat we can do is probably keep only the handles for ongoing transactions. But I will need to introduce a walker to get the ownership annotation from the host stage-2.",
      "parentUuid": "60d56758_dc7b0cb2",
      "revId": "39d5d9e55c8a360656ab9f30465fa9563b4a40d4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d96e03c5_e41dca04",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 885,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T12:49:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ha I see!\n\nFor the walker you wouldn\u0027t need anything specific and could just use kvm_pgtable_get_leaf(). But in any case there\u0027s still the need to store the list of handles somewhere so it doesn\u0027t really help us.",
      "parentUuid": "6cd9815f_8cb2250b",
      "revId": "39d5d9e55c8a360656ab9f30465fa9563b4a40d4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e56735c_47aa6ba3",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 885,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T13:26:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, giving more thoughts? Would that help to only store handles in the case where we expect a MEM_FRAG_TX?\n\nSo that we do not penalize too much other transactions with a linear search in a discontinuous array? (After few transactions, that\u0027s probably worst than just kvm_pgtable_get_leaf())?",
      "parentUuid": "d96e03c5_e41dca04",
      "revId": "39d5d9e55c8a360656ab9f30465fa9563b4a40d4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
